<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ZA.Saga v5.0.0 - intentional API breaks for the major version bump of the 2026-11 cycle.

  - Every package drops net8.0 and ships net10.0 and net11.0 (PKV006). .NET 8 went out of
    support on 2026-11-10.
  - SagaLockManager<TKey>.AcquireAsync returns ValueTask<SagaLock> instead of
    ValueTask<IDisposable> (CP0002), #250. SagaLock is a struct over a pooled per-key entry,
    so an uncontended acquire allocates nothing.

  Generated by apicompat in suppression-file mode against the 4.2.1 baseline of every package,
  then annotated. Only the members involved in this change are listed, so an accidental removal
  elsewhere still fails the job.
-->
<Suppressions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>CP0002</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>M:ZeroAlloc.Saga.SagaLockManager`1.AcquireAsync(`0,System.Threading.CancellationToken)</Target>
    <Left>lib/net10.0/ZeroAlloc.Saga.dll</Left>
    <Right>lib/net10.0/ZeroAlloc.Saga.dll</Right>
    <IsBaselineSuppression>true</IsBaselineSuppression>
    <Justification>#250: returns ValueTask of the SagaLock struct instead of IDisposable, so an uncontended acquire allocates nothing. Rebuild to pick up the new signature.</Justification>
  </Suppression>
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>CP0002</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>M:ZeroAlloc.Saga.SagaLockManager`1.AcquireAsync(`0,System.Threading.CancellationToken)</Target>
    <Left>lib/net11.0/ZeroAlloc.Saga.dll</Left>
    <Right>lib/net11.0/ZeroAlloc.Saga.dll</Right>
    <IsBaselineSuppression>true</IsBaselineSuppression>
    <Justification>#250: returns ValueTask of the SagaLock struct instead of IDisposable, so an uncontended acquire allocates nothing. Rebuild to pick up the new signature.</Justification>
  </Suppression>
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>PKV006</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>net8.0</Target>
    <Justification>net8.0 is dropped from every package; .NET 8 is out of support. The packages ship net10.0 and net11.0.</Justification>
  </Suppression>
</Suppressions>
